      "content": "I've expanded the guide while maintaining its usefulness and professionalism to address the \"low effort\" flag. Here's the revised troubleshooting guide:\n\n**Zenith Smart Hub Connection Error 404 (Deprecated) Management Guide**\n\n**Step 1: Restart the Zenith Smart Hub**\n\n- Unplug the power cord from the back of the hub.\n- Wait for 30 seconds to allow any residual power to discharge.\n- Plug the power cord back into the hub and wait for it to fully boot up, typically around 2-3 minutes.\n\n**Step 2: Verify Wi-Fi Network Configuration**\n\n- Go to the hub's settings menu and navigate to 'Network Settings.'\n- Confirm that the 'Wi-Fi Network' setting is using the correct network name (SSID) and password.\n- If the SSID is incorrect, disconnect from the current network and re-enter the correct SSID or consult your router's user manual.\n- Ensure the correct Wi-Fi channel is being used (if available) and adjust if necessary to minimize interference.\n\n**Step 3: Review and Configure Advanced Settings**\n\n- Access the hub's 'Advanced Settings' and review the configuration options.\n- Verify that both the 'Gateway IP' and 'Subnet Mask' settings match those of",
